meta {
  name: AutoReserveringHappyPathBom
  type: http
  seq: 61
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/web/bon/{{autoresBonnr}}/lijn
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  X-Auth-Token: {{authToken}}
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "artnr": "NOMALED.FUR1.2700.M.AB",
    "aantal": 1,
    "teLeveren": 1,
    "vprijs": 10.0
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 201
  res.body.bonnr: eq {{autoresBonnr}}
  res.body.gereserv: eq 1
}

docs {
  Iteratie C - automatische voorraadreservering, happy path on a BOM/
  "gemengd" article (artikel.soort = TRUE) that has enough stock at the
  top level and on every artlijn component in the shared LunaNew test DB
  at the time this test was written (verified via direct DB query during
  backend-coder implementation - see the handoff note for the exact
  before/after values). Asserts gereserv = teLeveren (full reservation).
  The resulting artikel.besteld-kl increment and the created
  bonlijn_productie rows (one per artlijn component, with their
  artikel.pbesteld-kl incremented) are NOT independently observable
  through the HTTP contract (no GET endpoint exposes besteld-kl/
  pbesteld-kl or bonlijn_productie) - they were confirmed via direct
  ABL/DB query during implementation, not by this Bruno request.
  Requires {{autoresBonnr}} (run "AutoReserveringSetupBon" first).
}
